[00:10.98]How do you say hello to someone you know?
[00:14.80]Do you smile? Do you touch the other person?
[00:19.78]Here are some ideas for travellers.
[00:23.92]This is how people in different countries welcome each other.
[00:28.48]Do you do different things in your country?
[00:32.82]In many countries in Asia, people bow their heads when they meet each other.
[00:40.06]This shows respect.
[00:42.36]In India, Nepal and Bangladesh, people bring their hands together in front of their heart and say 'Namaste'.
[00:52.96]When you greet a grandmother or grandfather or another older person in Turkey, you kiss their right hand and then place it on your forehead.
[01:05.46]They do this in the Philippines, too.
[01:09.98]The Maori people in New Zealand rub noses together when they meet.
[01:15.92]This is called the 'hongi'.
[01:19.80]In Malaysia, you put your hand on your heart and nod your head.
[01:25.76]Sometimes you also take the person's hands in your hands first.
[01:32.32]In Western countries, many people shake hands when they meet.
[01:38.52]Sometimes they just smile and say something like 'Hello!' or 'Hi!'
[01:45.92]In the US and in other countries, some people like using a 'fist bump' to greet another person.
[01:54.88]Both people make a fist, push their arm forward slowly and touch each other's fists.
[02:03.12]In many countries around the world, friends kiss each other on the cheek.
[02:09.84]In some countries they kiss one cheek, in others they kiss both cheeks and in some they kiss cheeks three times.
